  "description": "ZUYNAL crystallizes in the triclinic crystal system with space group P -1. Reported CIF formula moiety: C68 H82 Er4 N4 O32 Zn2 2+,2(C1 H4 O1),2(H2 O1),2(F6 P1 1-). From the CIF bond table, Er1 (Er) has 9 O neighbors; Er2 (Er) has 9 O neighbors; Zn1 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors; Er3 (Er) has 9 O neighbors; Er4 (Er) has 9 O neighbors; Zn2 (Zn) has 3 O neighbors. Oxygen-bridged metal-site graph: 5 pairs, 1 components; largest component is a chain with approximately linear metal-site arrangement. Computed bridged metal-metal separations span 3.338-4.095 Å (not direct metal-metal bonds). Computed M-O-M angles span 100.37-113.88°; individual values and O labels are in metal_framework.links. Article card reports molecular formula C70H90Er4F12N4O36P2Zn2. Explicit grouped units in the article formula/name: 10 OAc (explicit grouped unit in article compound name (structural notation)).",
